layout: tool.njk
tags: tools
permalink: "/tools/utm-builder/"
crumb: "UTM builder"
order: 2
heading: "UTM builder with GA4 channel checker"
standfirst: "Build clean, consistent UTM links, see which GA4 channel the traffic will land in before you send it, and generate a Final URL suffix with ValueTrack parameters for Google Ads."
title: "Free UTM Builder & GA4 Channel Checker | DigitalFadi"
description: "Free UTM builder that predicts the GA4 channel, enforces lowercase naming, and builds a Google Ads Final URL suffix with ValueTrack parameters."
faqs:
  - q: "What is a UTM builder?"
    a: "A UTM builder adds tracking parameters to the end of a link, such as utm_source, utm_medium and utm_campaign. When someone clicks the link, Google Analytics reads those parameters and records where the visit came from. A builder saves you typing them by hand and stops small mistakes, like a missing ampersand or a capital letter, from splitting your reports."
  - q: "Should I use UTM parameters on Google Ads campaigns?"
    a: "For Google Ads, turn on auto-tagging instead of adding google and cpc by hand. Auto-tagging adds a click ID that passes the campaign, ad group and keyword into GA4 automatically. UTMs are still useful in a Final URL suffix when another tool, such as a CRM or a form plugin, reads the source of a lead from the landing page URL."
  - q: "Are UTM parameters case sensitive?"
    a: "Yes. GA4 treats Email and email as two different values, so the same campaign ends up split across separate rows. The simplest fix is to keep every value lowercase and use hyphens instead of spaces, which this builder does by default."
  - q: "Why is my UTM traffic showing as Unassigned in GA4?"
    a: "GA4 sorts traffic into channels using fixed rules based on source and medium. If the medium is something GA4 does not recognise, such as qr, print or flyer, the session falls into Unassigned. Use a recognised medium like referral, email or affiliate, or create a custom channel group in GA4 that recognises your own values. The checker in this tool shows the likely channel before you publish the link."
  - q: "What is a Final URL suffix in Google Ads?"
    a: "It is a set of parameters that Google Ads adds to the end of your landing page URL on every click. It is set at account, campaign or ad group level and it does not start with a question mark. You can use ValueTrack parameters inside it, such as {keyword} or {device}, which Google replaces with real values at the moment of the click."
  - q: "Do UTM parameters hurt SEO?"
    a: "Not when the page has a canonical tag pointing at the clean URL, which most sites already have. The bigger risk is analytics, not SEO: never put UTMs on links between pages of your own site, because GA4 will treat the click as a new source and overwrite where the visitor really came from."
  - q: "Does this tool store my links?"
    a: "Your form values and saved links stay in this browser so they are still there next time. Nothing is uploaded or sent to any server, including mine. The Clear history button removes the saved links."
---
